s asset value ratio of 18 percent.","quote":"Rs 18,136 crore Net Debt Rs 99,080 crore GAV1 CRISIL AAA/Stable ICRA AAA/Stable Credit Rating 7.14% Interest Rate Net Debt to GAV: 18%","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_03082026173509_Letter.pdf","page":33.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"initiatives","statement":"DLF has executed 47 percent of its planned launches within two years and holds an upcoming medium-term pipeline of more than 60,000 crore rupees.","quote":"New Products : Launch Pipeline [Medium-Term] ~47% Launched in first 2 years; Healthy Pipeline for the medium term [ ~ 60k + crore]","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_03082026173509_Letter.pdf","page":12.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"risks","statement":"The company identified risks including earnings volatility, competition, execution delays, cost increases, and retention of skilled personnel.","quote":"The risks and uncertainties relating to such statements include, but are not limited to, earnings fluctuations, our ability to manage growth, competition, economic growth in India, ability to attract & retain highly skilled professionals, time & cost overruns on contracts","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_03082026173509_Letter.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"tone","statement":"positive","quote":"Past few year’s performance has laid down a strong foundation and clear visibility of future earnings and cash flows; future performance will only enhance this growth and financial position of the Group","doc_kind":"presentation","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_03082026173509_Letter.pdf","page":8.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"improved","statement":"Consolidated net profit for the quarter rose to INR 794 crores from INR 766 crores in the previous year's corresponding quarter.","quote":"Net profit for the quarter was INR 794 crores versus INR 766 crores in the same period last year.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"improved","statement":"DCCDL achieved a 10% year-over-year increase in revenue and more than 20% growth in net profit during the quarter.","quote":"Our consolidated revenue stood at INR1,917 crores, reflecting a growth of 10% year-over-year, yielding an EBITDA of INR 1,474 crores. Net profit continues to be a strong performance of INR 717 crores, a growth of over 20% year-over-year.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":4.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"deteriorated","statement":"Quarterly sales bookings dropped to INR 657 crores due to deferred launch timelines for the Aureva project.","quote":"New sales bookings for the quarter were INR 657 crores, reflecting the timing impact of deferment of our launch of Aureva, our senior living product.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"outlook","statement":"Management anticipates Midtown Plaza and Summit Plaza to reach stable rental operations by Q4 FY27, followed by the Goa mall around May or June of next year.","quote":"We expect both the malls to get into steady rental state by the first -- by the Q4 of FY27 and Goa to stabilize by about May/ June of next year.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":9.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"guidance","statement":"Management expects to achieve its full-year sales guidance despite a muted first quarter.","quote":"I mean this quarter from a pre-sales standpoint was a muted quarter and thank you for understanding the reason for that. And hopefully, we still stick to our broad guidance for sales for the year.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":13.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"demand","statement":"Large multinational and GCC clients seeking large spaces are restarting decision-making alongside steady domestic expansion.","quote":"The local Indian companies and normal ongoing expansion of the existing tenants have continued during this period. But the big boys who come where, say, 250,000 plus, 300,000 plus are the ones which have now started moving.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"costs","statement":"Revisions to minimum wages led to a slight increase of 2% to 2.5% in common area maintenance costs, which are passed through to tenants.","quote":"Yes, there has been a marginal impact on that. I would tend to think it's about 2%-2.5% of CAM cost, which has gone up. There has been no pushback from the tenants because this is a national law","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":7.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"margins","statement":"DLF maintains an estimated embedded gross margin potential of approximately INR 39,000 crores.","quote":"Just to remind, the gross margin potential as it stands today, is approximately INR 39,000 crores.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":3.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"capex","statement":"Capex execution for Downtown Gurgaon Phase 2 and Downtown Chennai Phase 2 is moving forward at full pace.","quote":"Our capex program on Downtown Gurgaon Phase 2 and Downtown Chennai Phase 2 are going at full speed and the leasing here in Gurgaon is about 40%.","doc_kind":"transcript","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DLF_07082026151631_Letter.pdf","page":4.0,"kind":"extracted"},{"field":"debt","statement":"DLF closed the first quarter with 